// EnumBox for the NeoDDS enum-TypeObject interop probe (log-service Task 2 debt; ADR 0082 §9.0).
//
// The question this answers: NeoDDS's (:enum ...) member emits TK_INT32 in the TypeObject, because
// the serializer cannot yet emit a real MinimalEnumeratedType (equivalence-hash takes a
// minimal-struct-type only). A conformant peer whose IDL declares an `enum` presents TK_ENUM. Under
// strict XTypes type-consistency the two are structurally different types (the ADR 0009 defect
// class). Does a real RTI Connext peer REJECT the match, or TOLERATE it (Connext's default
// TypeConsistencyEnforcement is ALLOW_TYPE_COERCION, and an enum is int32-backed)?
//
// The answer decides whether log-service Phase B can ship LogEvent with an enum-as-int32 against
// strict Connext, or whether the MinimalEnumeratedType serializer must land first.
//
// Kind is a real IDL enum -> TK_ENUM on this side. NeoDDS's matching enum-box type declares the same
// member as (:enum ...) -> TK_INT32. Same topic name "EnumBox", same registered type name "EnumBox",
// @key long id, so the enum member is the ONLY intended difference.

enum Kind {
    KIND_TRACE,
    KIND_INFO,
    KIND_ERROR
};

@final
struct EnumBox {
    @key long id;
    Kind kind;
};
